  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Focusing on rural development, the Project aims to improve sustainable livelihoods and formal employment for both refugees and host communities. Specifically, it targets the employment status, employability, and working conditions of Syrian Men and Women Agricultural Workers (SMAWs) while boosting the business viability of agricultural enterprises and cooperatives. Key outputs include registering SMAWs in the Work Permit Exemption System, delivering employability support services, providing busi</narrative>
  </description>
